$$
\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\frac{1}{0-0-C}=1\,⇒\,C=-1\,.\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, the particular solution of $y' = (1-2x)y^2$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1$ is

$$
y    =   \dfrac {1} {x^2 - x - (-1)} = \dfrac {1} {x^2 - x + 1}\,.
$$

